  "renderer_requirements": [
    {
      "area": "Source identities and mixed content",
      "requirements": "Use a B10 PreTeXt adapter rather than the CNXML renderer. Preserve original xml:id and label separately: 12 XML IDs plus 7 labels in chapter 0; graphs-evensum labels the latex-image child, not its image parent. Most paragraphs have no IDs: derive documented path keys and distinguish generated reader anchors from original IDs. Preserve all own text/tails; valid HTML equivalents are needed for p enclosing lists, display math or sidebyside blocks."
    },
    {
      "area": "TeX mathematics",
      "requirements": "There are 102 m and 3 me nodes, not source MathML. Bind exact raw TeX, owners, slot order and tails before conversion; preserve shared macros, notably N and st. Keep formulas, sets, pairs, recurrence initial conditions, subscripts and table direction LTR. The sole English text token inside math is \\text{ and }; retaining it with a Punjabi explanation is the simplest exact option; translating it requires a specific reversible ledger, not blanket text normalization."
    },
    {
      "area": "Numeric answers and interactions",
      "requirements": "Preserve five ungraded response prompts as ungraded. The sixth exercise is numeric: three visible var slots correspond positionally to setup var values 6,10,15, with number condition followed by fallback regex .* and exact source feedback. Translate all feedback, do not expose Correct beside wrong answers or misbind slots. Include component=runestone reading questions even in an offline reader. A static accessible question/answer reveal is possible if accurately labeled; do not promise external grading or falsely claim missing WeBWorK functionality."
    },
    {
      "area": "Table",
      "requirements": "Preserve 2x6 cell matrix and source column/right and row/bottom minor-rule attributes; no CNXML CALS conversion assumptions. Matrix is [n,1,2,3,4,...] and [a_n,1,3,6,10,...]. Retain literal ellipses, source indices and formula linkage without inventing a different sequence."
    },
    {
      "area": "Graphs",
      "requirements": "Use pinned canonical generated-assets/rs SVG bytes or verify a deterministic derivation against their TikZ. The web generated directory does not supply these canonical files locally; rs SVGs are tracked and available. Each is 76x73, six vertex labels, no external references. Do not substitute the Indonesian web SVGs (77x75, different bytes) or mirror geometry. Bind sum-7 edges {1,6},{2,5},{3,4} and even-sum edges {1,5},{2,6},{1,3},{4,6},{2,4},{3,5}. Keep both source descriptions for first graph; second graph has only shortdescription in English."
    },
    {
      "area": "Cross-references",
      "requirements": "Preserve sec_intro-structures as local Section 0.2; forward ch_sequences and ch_graphtheory mean Chapters 4 and 2. Do not make dead local links or falsely claim their Punjabi pages exist. Use clearly marked source/pending destinations until translated. Keep cross-references text=type-global metadata and actual book numbering."
    },
    {
      "area": "Footnotes, glossary and metadata",
      "requirements": "Retain both inline footnotes, including the nursery-rhyme joke and toy-problem caveat, with exact owner and return links. Translate 33 index records / 38 h plus 2 see strings as index metadata, not accidental body prose; preserve index hierarchy and term markup including math within n-tuple. Keep titlepage names, institutions, dates, dedication, acknowledgements and two author attribution lines, plus all frontmatter URLs and QR context."
    },
    {
      "area": "Frontmatter assets and claims",
      "requirements": "Keep the canonical 100x142 cover/logo and 200x200 QR original; source QR shortdescription spells https://discrete/openmathbooks.org while adjacent URL is https://discrete.openmathbooks.org/. Preserve the raw erroneous description separately if correcting accessible text. Do not substitute the Indonesian QR or URLs. Do not copy analytics, service credentials, external runtime scripts or live grading as incidental renderer behavior. Source access, interactive-feature, edition and publication statements remain pinned-source claims."
    },
    {
      "area": "Local implementation availability",
      "requirements": "Both repositories pin PreTeXt 2.27.0. The inspected system Python has lxml but not pretext or latex2mathml; xsl/core/pretext-html.xsl imported by custom XSL is not present at that path. No installation/build attempted. Existing canonical SVGs avoid a first-unit TikZ rebuild, but a verified TeX-to-MathML or local math runtime still needs a scoped implementation decision."
